# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of the
# checkout platform's default — silences the "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warning every commit printed on Windows checkouts (docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md).
# Git still checks files out using the platform's native line endings
# locally (core.autocrlf), this only fixes what's actually stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish or intentionally-CRLF file types some tools still expect CRLF for.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
